[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: System Requirements
UID: SYSREQ-DOC
VERSION: 1.0

[GRAMMAR]
ELEMENTS:
- TAG: REQUIREMENT
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: TITLE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: STATEMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: RATIONALE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  RELATIONS:
  - TYPE: Parent

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYSREQ-001
TITLE: Test Documentation Generation
STATEMENT: The system shall generate test plan documentation from structured data files.
RATIONALE: Automated generation ensures consistency and reduces manual documentation effort.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYSREQ-002
TITLE: Template-Based Rendering
STATEMENT: The system shall support template-based rendering using Jinja2-like syntax.
RATIONALE: Templates provide flexibility and allow customization of output format without code changes.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYSREQ-003
TITLE: Schema Validation
STATEMENT: The system shall validate input data against JSON schemas before processing.
RATIONALE: Schema validation ensures data integrity and catches errors early in the process.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYSREQ-004
TITLE: Multiple Verification Methods
STATEMENT: The system shall support multiple verification methods including test, analysis, demonstration, and inspection.
RATIONALE: Different requirements may require different verification approaches based on their nature.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYSREQ-005
TITLE: Multiple Output Formats
STATEMENT: The system shall support generating documentation in multiple output formats.
RATIONALE: Different stakeholders may require different documentation formats (Markdown, AsciiDoc).

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYSREQ-006
TITLE: Command-Line Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall provide a command-line interface for automation and scripting.
RATIONALE: CLI enables integration with build systems and CI/CD pipelines.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYSREQ-007
TITLE: Requirements Traceability
STATEMENT: The system shall support traceability from test cases to requirements.
RATIONALE: Traceability ensures all requirements are verified and enables impact analysis.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYSREQ-008
TITLE: Modular Template System
STATEMENT: The system shall support separate templates for container-level and test-case-level documentation.
RATIONALE: Separation of concerns allows independent customization of different documentation sections.
